# INERT ON GITHUB PAGES. Kept because it is the whole header policy in one file:
# if this site ever moves back to Cloudflare Pages (or to Netlify, which reads the
# same format) it starts working again untouched.
#
# GitHub Pages serves no custom headers at all and offers no way to add them, so
# on the current host none of the rules below apply. What is actually lost:
#   - X-Frame-Options / Referrer-Policy / Permissions-Policy — no equivalent.
#     A <meta http-equiv> tag cannot set them; only CSP works that way.
#   - The Cache-Control tuning. Pages sends a short max-age with an ETag for
#     everything, so hashed /_astro/ assets get revalidated instead of served
#     from cache for a year. Correct, just slower than it needs to be.
#
# Cloudflare Pages headers. Copied verbatim from public/ into dist/ at build time.
# Static-hosting concerns only; nothing here depends on an account.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()

# Astro fingerprints these filenames, so they can be cached indefinitely.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Media filenames are stable rather than hashed, so revalidate daily. The heavy
# animated WebPs are only fetched on user intent anyway (see MotionMedia).
/media/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/og/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# The résumé is replaced without a filename change, so don't cache it hard.
/resume.pdf
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
